jected 3-litre M186 six-cylinder engine was designated W112. Full-size luxury car 1960 rear-wheel-drive 890 850 760 320 198 front completed not completed not completed virtual-car Product Data Cars mercedes',''),(336,'',0,'/Sample Content/Documents/classic-car-2016-3857.pdf','asset','document','document',1,1563871131,1566567215,2,2,'ID: 336  \nPath: /Sample Content/Documents/classic-car-2016-3857.pdf  \nclassic-car-2016-3857.pdf RESIDENTIAL RESEARCH CLASSIC CAR SPECIAL Luxury Investment Index 2016 FERRARI SETS NEW AUCTION RECORD CLASSIC CAR PERFORMANCE FOCUS BUILDING CLASSIC CAR COLLECTION WEALTH REPORT UPDATE LUXURY INVESTMENT INDEX 2016 Quality takes centre stage luxury markets let off steam Classic cars set new records auction but buyers are becoming more discerning the asset classes include the Knight Luxury Investment Index (KFLII) classic cars arguably capture the imagination more than anything else. Not only has their performance terms price over past decade been staggering but thrill owning such visceral and often historic vehicles hard beat. I’m therefore delighted that this edition KFLII focuses these amazing machines including host fascinating facts and figures from our data partner HAGI. hope you enjoy reading much did writing and researching it. ANDREW SHIRLEY The Wealth Report Editor Classic cars were once again top performing luxury asset annual basis (see graphic page according latest figures from Knight Frank Luxury Investment Index (KFLII). While overall value KFLII increased just months end March 2016 lowest annual increase since first quarter 2010 outperformed with 17% surge. Fine wine saw second strongest growth with rare coins third position rising 6%. The Bordeaux market bouncing back strongly after falling sharply between 2012 2014 while north Italian wines are continuing enjoy annual double-digit growth explains Nick Martin Wine Owners which compiles Knight Frank Fine Wine Icons Index. Coins remain strong demand investment asset says Keith H